20217 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The buy function lets a bettor purchase shares in one market outcome\056 It calls \137credit\054 which uses LsLmsr\056sharesBought to calculate the shares through repeated full\055book cost calculations\056 This applies to every bettor\054 including users of the gasless buyWithAuthorization route\056\nAll supported market configurations should be tradable on Base at normal stake sizes\056 In particular\054 MAX\137OUTCOMES allows 32 outcomes so a five\055leg binary parlay can be created\054 and the gas benchmark treats a 100 USDC buy in this configuration as supported\056\nHowever\054 the limit was chosen against Base\047s 100M block gas limit instead of its 16\054777\054216 per\055transaction gas cap\056 The repository\047s own optimized benchmark shows that the 32\055outcome\054 100 USDC buy uses more than 25M gas\056 A user cannot raise the transaction gas limit to compensate\072 Base rejects a regular transaction above the cap\054 while a transaction at or below it runs out of gas\056 The authorized and basket\055buy paths do at least the same pricing work and therefore do not provide a workaround\056\nAn ordinary failure scenario is\072\nA creator deploys a five\055leg binary parlay with 32 outcomes\054 which passes the MAX\137OUTCOMES check\056\nA bettor submits a direct 100 USDC buy\056\nThe buy needs more than 25M gas\054 so it cannot execute under Base\047s 16\054777\054216 transaction cap and reverts\056\nThe market remains deployed\054 but its advertised trading flow is unavailable for this normal stake size\056)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 20218 0 R
     /Pg 7444 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

