20570 0 obj
  << /ActualText (sharesBoughtImpl converts a user\047s stake into shares by searching for the largest share amount whose LMSR cost is no greater than the stake\056 Regular and gasless buys reach it through MarketCore\056\137credit\054 while parlay basket buys use the equivalent basketSharesImpl flow\056 These entry points are available to ordinary bettors\056\nThe search should start with an upper bound that is known to be unaffordable\056 Bisection can then return the largest affordable amount\054 after which the market credits those shares and pulls the user\047s full stake\056\nHowever\054 priceBpsImpl rounds prices down to whole basis points\056 When an outcome\047s real price is positive but below one basis point\054 it returns zero\056 bracket then changes that zero to one basis point and derives the search limit from it\072)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 20571 0 R
     /Pg 16116 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

20571 0 obj
  << /K [ 20570 0 R ]
     /P 20578 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 16116 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

20572 0 obj
  << /ActualText (uint256 priceBpsValue \075 Math\056max\050priceBpsImpl\050outcome\054 q\054 alphaBps\054 bMin\051\054 1\051\073\nuint256 hiBound \075 Math\056mulDiv\050target\054 BPS\137DENOM\054 priceBpsValue\051 \053 1\073)
     /K [ 12 ]
     /P 20573 0 R
     /Pg 16116 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

20573 0 obj
  << /K [ 20572 0 R ]
     /P 20578 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 16116 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

20574 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Rounding the price up makes hiBound too small\054 so it is not necessarily an upper bound at all\056 sharesBoughtImpl never checks whether that bound is unaffordable and cannot find any larger fill\056 The basket path has the same issue when all selected cell prices round to zero\056 MarketCore\056buy and MarketParlay\056buyBasket still transfer and account for the full stake\054 with no refund for the underfill\056\nFor example\054 consider a 6\055decimal binary market with alphaBps \075 300\054 bMin \075 1\054000\054000\054 inventory \1331\054000\054000\054000\054000\054 0\135\054 and a 1\054000\054000 stake on the second outcome\072\nThe second outcome\047s real price is about 0\056000000924 basis points\054 but priceBpsImpl returns zero\056\nbracket substitutes one basis point and caps the search near 10\054000\054000\054000 share units\056\nA fill of 250\054000\054000\054000 share units is still affordable and costs only about 51\054590 units under costImpl\054 but bisection cannot reach it\056\nWith a permissive minSharesOut\054 the market credits the capped fill and pulls the full 1\054000\054000 stake\056 The bettor receives far less payout exposure if the outcome wins\054 while the excess collateral remains in the market\056)
     /K [ 13 ]
     /P 20575 0 R
     /Pg 16116 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

