20619 0 obj
  << /ActualText (However\054 the signed message has no deadline\054 and the direct setAllowed\050\051 does not advance nonce\056 As a result\054 a signed update that has not been submitted yet stays valid indefinitely\054 and the owner cannot invalidate it with a direct call\056\nFor example\072\nThe owner signs SetAllowed\050\133Alice\135\054 true\054 nonce \075 1\051 and hands it to the relayer\056\nBefore it is submitted\054 the owner decides Alice must not bet anymore and calls setAllowed\050\133Alice\135\054 false\051 directly\056 nonce is still 1\056\nThe relayer \050or anyone holding the signature\051 submits the signed message\056 The nonce still matches\054 so Alice is allowed again and the owner\047s latest decision is silently reverted\056\nNote that the codebase already handles this case elsewhere\072 CreatorResolver and MarketCore\056sweep\050\051 both consume the current nonce on the direct path\054 so an older outstanding signature is invalidated\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 20620 0 R
     /Pg 17352 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

